Q: Refresh page when it passes width A: <p>Sounds like you need to refresh content not just change styling. If that is the case you will want to use <code>window.matchMedia()</code>.</p>

<p>Here's how you use it:</p>

<p><code>var mq = window.matchMedia( "(min-width: 500px)" );</code></p>

<p>The matches property returns true or false depending on the query result, e.g.</p>

<pre><code>if (mq.matches) {
  // window width is at least 500px
} else {
  // window width is less than 500px
}
</code></pre>

<p>This snippet was <a href="https://www.sitepoint.com/javascript-media-queries/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">taken from here</a>.</p>
